  add('en', {

    // 1) kaynakli-imalat-nedir
    blog_kaynakli_imalat_nedir_title: 'What Is Welded Manufacturing? Core Processes and Standards | ArmaWeld',
    blog_kaynakli_imalat_nedir_meta_desc: 'What is welded manufacturing, what processes does it cover, and how is it executed under EN ISO 3834-2 and EN 1090? A technical guide from ArmaWeld in Konya, Türkiye.',
    blog_kaynakli_imalat_nedir_og_title: 'What Is Welded Manufacturing? Core Processes and Standards',
    blog_kaynakli_imalat_nedir_tag: 'Welded Manufacturing · Fundamentals',
    blog_kaynakli_imalat_nedir_h1: 'What Is Welded Manufacturing? Core Processes and Standards',
    blog_kaynakli_imalat_nedir_read: '8 min read',
    blog_kaynakli_imalat_nedir_author: 'ArmaWeld Engineering',
    blog_kaynakli_imalat_nedir_breadcrumb3: 'What Is Welded Manufacturing',
    blog_kaynakli_imalat_nedir_s0: '<p><strong>Welded manufacturing</strong> is the production method in which metal parts are permanently joined using heat and/or pressure, usually with a filler material, to form a final product or structure. Chassis, pressure vessels, structural steel, defense platforms and agricultural machinery are produced using welded manufacturing. In Konya and across Türkiye’s industrial hubs, welded manufacturing is a discipline where engineering design, material selection, production process and quality control are fully integrated.</p><p>This article examines the core steps of welded manufacturing, the most common welding processes, quality requirements and the <span class="tag-inline">EN ISO 3834-2</span> and <span class="tag-inline">EN 1090</span> standards from a hands-on perspective.</p>',
    blog_kaynakli_imalat_nedir_s1: '<h2>1. Core Steps of Welded Manufacturing</h2><p>A welded manufacturing project is far more than the welding step alone. From design inputs to final delivery, multiple stages are managed under tight discipline.</p><ul><li><strong>Engineering design:</strong> Load analysis, material selection, weld details and tolerances are defined.</li><li><strong>Material procurement:</strong> Steel plate, sections and consumables with EN 10204 3.1 certificates are sourced.</li><li><strong>Cutting and forming:</strong> Laser/plasma cutting, press brake forming and machining.</li><li><strong>Pre-weld preparation:</strong> Joint preparation, cleaning, preheating and tacking.</li><li><strong>Welding:</strong> Performed by qualified welders following an approved WPS.</li><li><strong>Inspection:</strong> Visual, PT, MT, UT or RT NDT.</li><li><strong>Surface finishing & shipment:</strong> Blasting, painting or galvanizing followed by delivery.</li></ul>',
    blog_kaynakli_imalat_nedir_s2: '<h2>2. Common Welding Processes</h2><p>The selected method depends on material, thickness, production volume and quality expectations.</p><table class="data-table"><thead><tr><th>Process</th><th>ISO No.</th><th>Typical Use</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>MIG/MAG (GMAW)</td><td>135/138</td><td>Structural steel, chassis, general fabrication</td></tr><tr><td>FCAW</td><td>136</td><td>Heavy sections, site welding</td></tr><tr><td>TIG (GTAW)</td><td>141</td><td>Stainless, aluminum, root passes</td></tr><tr><td>SMAW</td><td>111</td><td>Repairs, isolated points</td></tr><tr><td>SAW</td><td>121</td><td>Heavy plate, pressure vessels, pipes</td></tr></tbody></table>',
    blog_kaynakli_imalat_nedir_s3: '<h2>3. Quality and Traceability Standards</h2><p>In professional <strong>welded manufacturing</strong>, every weld must be traceable. <span class="tag-inline">EN ISO 3834-2</span> requires assigning a welding coordinator, managing WPS/WPQR, controlled consumable storage and inspection records. For structural steel, <span class="tag-inline">EN 1090-2</span> applies and quality is set per EXC1–EXC4 execution classes.</p><div class="callout"><p><strong>Practical note:</strong> All ArmaWeld projects are executed under EN ISO 3834-2 with a welding engineer in coordination, and digital traceability links every weld to the welder ID and consumable batch.</p></div>',
    blog_kaynakli_imalat_nedir_s4: '<h2>4. Welded Manufacturing in Konya and ArmaWeld</h2><p>Konya hosts one of Türkiye’s strongest metalworking and machinery ecosystems. The city’s welded manufacturing capacity for agricultural machinery, automotive sub-industry, defense and energy is increasing every year. ArmaWeld brings engineering, welded manufacturing, NDT inspection and surface finishing under one roof, offering subcontract and turn-key solutions. ArmaWeld delivers up to EN 1090 EXC3 quality on high-strength steels, stainless alloys, aluminum and special armor steels with certified welders.</p>',
    blog_kaynakli_imalat_nedir_cta_h3: 'Get a quote for your welded manufacturing project',
    blog_kaynakli_imalat_nedir_cta_p: 'Design, welding, NDT and shipment from the Konya production facility — under one roof.',
    blog_kaynakli_imalat_nedir_cta_btn: 'Request a Quote →',

    // 2) konya-kaynakli-imalat
    blog_konya_kaynakli_imalat_title: 'Welded Manufacturing in Konya: Production at Türkiye’s Industrial Hub | ArmaWeld',
    blog_konya_kaynakli_imalat_meta_desc: 'The strength of Konya’s welded manufacturing sector, ArmaWeld’s production infrastructure in the Konya OIZ, sectors and capacities. EN 1090 and EN ISO 3834-2 production.',
    blog_konya_kaynakli_imalat_og_title: 'Welded Manufacturing in Konya: Production at Türkiye’s Industrial Hub',
    blog_konya_kaynakli_imalat_tag: 'Konya · Industry',
    blog_konya_kaynakli_imalat_h1: 'Welded Manufacturing in Konya: Production at Türkiye’s Industrial Hub',
    blog_konya_kaynakli_imalat_read: '7 min read',
    blog_konya_kaynakli_imalat_author: 'ArmaWeld Engineering',
    blog_konya_kaynakli_imalat_breadcrumb3: 'Welded Manufacturing in Konya',
    blog_konya_kaynakli_imalat_s0: '<p>The <strong>welded manufacturing</strong> sector in Konya has become one of Türkiye’s fastest-growing metalworking ecosystems over the last 20 years. Together with Konya’s 1st and 2nd Organized Industrial Zones, the city is a key production base for agricultural machinery, automotive sub-industry, defense and machinery manufacturing. This article covers Konya’s <strong>welded manufacturing</strong> capacity, ArmaWeld services and why producing in Konya delivers value to customers.</p>',
    blog_konya_kaynakli_imalat_s1: '<h2>1. Konya’s Industrial Advantages</h2><p>Konya is a strategic production hub thanks to both its geography and industrial ecosystem. Located in the heart of Anatolia, it offers efficient access to the domestic market and to export channels via the port of Mersin.</p><ul><li>3,000+ metalworking companies and a developed supply chain</li><li>Strong university ecosystem with engineering capacity</li><li>Fast access to raw materials and consumables</li><li>Lower logistics costs</li><li>Skilled welder and technician pool</li></ul>',
    blog_konya_kaynakli_imalat_s2: '<h2>2. ArmaWeld Production Capability</h2><p>At its Konya facility, ArmaWeld delivers <strong>welded fabrication</strong> for structural steel, defense and special machinery. Certificate and process scope are shared rather than machine counts:</p><table class="data-table"><thead><tr><th>Area</th><th>Scope</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Certification</td><td>EN 1090 EXC3 · EN ISO 3834-2</td></tr><tr><td>Welding methods</td><td>MIG/MAG · TIG · FCAW · SAW</td></tr><tr><td>Material groups</td><td>S235–S960QL · Strenx/HARDOX · Stainless · Al</td></tr><tr><td>Cutting & bending</td><td>CNC plasma/laser · press brake bending · rolling</td></tr><tr><td>NDT</td><td>VT · PT · MT · UT (ISO 9712 L2)</td></tr><tr><td>Quote SLA</td><td>48 hours · NDA standard</td></tr></tbody></table>',
    blog_konya_kaynakli_imalat_s3: '<h2>3. Sectors Served</h2><p>From the Konya base, a wide spectrum of sectors is served across Türkiye and export markets:</p><ul><li><strong>Defense:</strong> Armored vehicle subframes, tactical wheeled platforms</li><li><strong>Agricultural machinery:</strong> Plows, seeders, trailers, combine chassis</li><li><strong>Energy:</strong> Wind turbine components, hydroelectric cabinets</li><li><strong>Construction:</strong> EN 1090 EXC2/EXC3 structural steel</li><li><strong>Mining:</strong> Conveyors, screening equipment, wear plates</li></ul>',
    blog_konya_kaynakli_imalat_s4: '<h2>4. Why Produce From Konya?</h2><p>Producing from Konya offers a meaningful cost and time advantage for exports to Europe and the Middle East. ArmaWeld operates a quality system applying EN 1090, EN ISO 3834-2 and customer-specific standards. Both subcontract and turn-key options are offered to customers searching for a <strong>welding company in Konya</strong>. ArmaWeld’s throughput, engineering capability and digital traceability infrastructure make Konya not only a production address but a true engineering partner.</p>',
    blog_konya_kaynakli_imalat_cta_h3: 'Quality welded manufacturing from Konya',
    blog_konya_kaynakli_imalat_cta_p: 'Contact us for technical feasibility, pricing and prototype production for your project.',
    blog_konya_kaynakli_imalat_cta_btn: 'Request a Quote →',

    // 3) savunma-sanayi-kaynakli-imalat
    blog_savunma_sanayi_kaynakli_imalat_title: 'Welded Manufacturing for Defense: STANAG, MIL-STD and Special Steels | ArmaWeld',
    blog_savunma_sanayi_kaynakli_imalat_meta_desc: 'Welded manufacturing for the defense industry: STANAG 4569 armor levels, MIL-STD-1941, ballistic steel welding and quality requirements.',
    blog_savunma_sanayi_kaynakli_imalat_og_title: 'Welded Manufacturing for Defense: STANAG, MIL-STD and Special Steels',
    blog_savunma_sanayi_kaynakli_imalat_tag: 'Defense · Ballistic Steel',
    blog_savunma_sanayi_kaynakli_imalat_h1: 'Welded Manufacturing for Defense: STANAG, MIL-STD and Special Steels',
    blog_savunma_sanayi_kaynakli_imalat_read: '10 min read',
    blog_savunma_sanayi_kaynakli_imalat_author: 'ArmaWeld Engineering',
    blog_savunma_sanayi_kaynakli_imalat_breadcrumb3: 'Defense Industry Welding',
    blog_savunma_sanayi_kaynakli_imalat_s0: '<p><strong>Defense welded manufacturing</strong> requires a discipline very different from ordinary structural steel work. Ballistic steels, high-carbon alloys with narrow preheat windows and the requirement for certified welding personnel define this domain. ArmaWeld delivers <strong>defense welding</strong> for armored vehicles and defense platforms from Konya. This article covers STANAG, MIL-STD standards and welding processes for special steels.</p>',
    blog_savunma_sanayi_kaynakli_imalat_s1: '<h2>1. STANAG 4569 Ballistic Protection Levels</h2><p>NATO standard STANAG 4569 defines protection levels of armored vehicles against ballistic and blast threats. Welding details must be designed in accordance with these levels.</p><table class="data-table"><thead><tr><th>Level</th><th>Threat</th><th>Typical Thickness</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Level 1</td><td>5.56×45 mm</td><td>6–8 mm</td></tr><tr><td>Level 2</td><td>7.62×39 mm</td><td>10–12 mm</td></tr><tr><td>Level 3</td><td>7.62×51 mm AP</td><td>14–16 mm</td></tr><tr><td>Level 4</td><td>14.5×114 mm AP</td><td>30–35 mm</td></tr></tbody></table>',
    blog_savunma_sanayi_kaynakli_imalat_s2: '<h2>2. Welding Challenges of Ballistic Steels</h2><p>Ballistic steels such as ARMOX, MARS, RAMOR and SECURE are tempered for high hardness, leaving very narrow heat input limits.</p><ul><li><strong>Maximum heat input:</strong> typically 1.0–1.5 kJ/mm</li><li><strong>Preheat:</strong> 100–150°C depending on thickness</li><li><strong>Interpass temperature:</strong> max 200°C</li><li><strong>Filler:</strong> austenitic (e.g. AWS E307, E309LMo) preferred</li><li><strong>Hydrogen control:</strong> H5 or H4 class with controlled storage</li></ul>',
    blog_savunma_sanayi_kaynakli_imalat_s3: '<h2>3. Quality and Personnel Certification</h2><p>For defense projects every welder must be qualified to the relevant WPS under <span class="tag-inline">EN ISO 9606-1</span> or customer-specific standards. ArmaWeld’s defense QC flow:</p><ol><li>WPS/PQR alignment with the customer</li><li>Consumable batch checks (certificate, hydrogen level)</li><li>Preheat and temperature logs</li><li>100% visual inspection plus sampled UT/MT for every weld</li><li>Ballistic test panel verification</li></ol><div class="callout"><p><strong>Important:</strong> Defense projects almost always require digital traceability records from consumable batch to finished product, both by the customer and the end user.</p></div>',
    blog_savunma_sanayi_kaynakli_imalat_s4: '<h2>4. ArmaWeld Defense Track Record</h2><p>ArmaWeld provides <strong>defense welding</strong> from Konya as an engineering partner to prime contractors and OEMs. Armored vehicle substructure parts, tactical wheeled platform chassis, ammunition boxes and special equipment are part of the production portfolio. Every project runs under EN ISO 3834-2 with welding engineer coordination and a digital traceability infrastructure.</p>',
    blog_savunma_sanayi_kaynakli_imalat_cta_h3: 'ArmaWeld for your defense project',
    blog_savunma_sanayi_kaynakli_imalat_cta_p: 'Get a technical proposal for ballistic steel welding, armored vehicle substructures and defense platforms.',
    blog_savunma_sanayi_kaynakli_imalat_cta_btn: 'Request a Quote →',

    // 4) celik-konstruksiyon-imalat
    blog_celik_konstruksiyon_imalat_title: 'Steel Structure Manufacturing: From Design to Erection | ArmaWeld',
    blog_celik_konstruksiyon_imalat_meta_desc: 'Steel structure manufacturing processes, EN 1090 execution classes, shop and site welding requirements. A technical guide from ArmaWeld.',
    blog_celik_konstruksiyon_imalat_og_title: 'Steel Structure Manufacturing: From Design to Erection',
    blog_celik_konstruksiyon_imalat_tag: 'Steel Structures · EN 1090',
    blog_celik_konstruksiyon_imalat_h1: 'Steel Structure Manufacturing: From Design to Erection',
    blog_celik_konstruksiyon_imalat_read: '8 min read',
    blog_celik_konstruksiyon_imalat_author: 'ArmaWeld Engineering',
    blog_celik_konstruksiyon_imalat_breadcrumb3: 'Steel Structures',
    blog_celik_konstruksiyon_imalat_s0: '<p><strong>Steel structure manufacturing</strong> covers the production of primary load-bearing systems for industrial buildings, warehouses, bridges, factory roofs and special structures. When every step from design to erection is executed in accordance with EN 1090, the best balance of safety and cost is achieved. This article covers the core steps of <strong>structural steel fabrication</strong> and the solutions ArmaWeld delivers from Konya.</p>',
    blog_celik_konstruksiyon_imalat_s1: '<h2>1. Design and Detailing</h2><p>In modern steel projects, engineering is performed with 3D BIM tools. Tekla Structures, IDEA StatiCa and SDS/2 automatically generate connection details, bolt lists and shop drawings. ArmaWeld can generate detail drawings from customer-supplied IFC or DWG files and works in coordination with structural design offices.</p>',
    blog_celik_konstruksiyon_imalat_s2: '<h2>2. Shop Fabrication</h2><p>Per EN 1090-2, shop processes include cutting, drilling, forming, assembly and welding. The higher the execution class (EXC), the tighter the tolerance, traceability and inspection requirements.</p><table class="data-table"><thead><tr><th>EXC Class</th><th>Typical Structure</th><th>NDT Coverage</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>EXC1</td><td>Agricultural building, small warehouse</td><td>VT only</td></tr><tr><td>EXC2</td><td>Industrial building</td><td>VT + 5–10% NDT</td></tr><tr><td>EXC3</td><td>Bridges, crane runways</td><td>VT + 10–20% NDT</td></tr><tr><td>EXC4</td><td>Special-risk structures</td><td>VT + 100% NDT</td></tr></tbody></table>',
    blog_celik_konstruksiyon_imalat_s3: '<h2>3. Welding and Quality</h2><p>The most common welding processes for structural steel are MAG (135), FCAW (136) and SAW (121). For each process, an approved <span class="tag-inline">WPS</span> and PQR record is maintained. Welders are qualified under EN ISO 9606-1, with daily monitoring of shop temperature and consumable storage. At ArmaWeld, every weld is recorded digitally and linked to a unique welder ID.</p>',
    blog_celik_konstruksiyon_imalat_s4: '<h2>4. Site Erection and Delivery</h2><p>Shop-fabricated modules are shipped to site and joined with bolted or welded connections. Site welds require wind shielding, preheating and visual inspection. ArmaWeld can organize site erection crews on customer demand and coordinates blasting, painting and galvanizing. Konya-based production delivers competitive lead times across Türkiye and export markets.</p>',
    blog_celik_konstruksiyon_imalat_cta_h3: 'Get a quote for your steel structure project',
    blog_celik_konstruksiyon_imalat_cta_p: 'Design, fabrication and erection from the EN 1090 EXC2/EXC3 certified shop.',
    blog_celik_konstruksiyon_imalat_cta_btn: 'Request a Quote →',

    // 5) endustriyel-kaynak-hizmeti
    blog_endustriyel_kaynak_hizmeti_title: 'Industrial Welding Services: Plant and Factory Applications | ArmaWeld',
    blog_endustriyel_kaynak_hizmeti_meta_desc: 'Industrial welding services: plant, factory and process equipment, on-site and shop welding. From Konya-based ArmaWeld.',
    blog_endustriyel_kaynak_hizmeti_og_title: 'Industrial Welding Services: Plant and Factory Applications',
    blog_endustriyel_kaynak_hizmeti_tag: 'Industrial Welding · Plant',
    blog_endustriyel_kaynak_hizmeti_h1: 'Industrial Welding Services: Plant and Factory Applications',
    blog_endustriyel_kaynak_hizmeti_read: '7 min read',
    blog_endustriyel_kaynak_hizmeti_author: 'ArmaWeld Engineering',
    blog_endustriyel_kaynak_hizmeti_breadcrumb3: 'Industrial Welding',
    blog_endustriyel_kaynak_hizmeti_s0: '<p><strong>Industrial welding services</strong> play a critical role in the manufacturing, modification and maintenance of in-plant equipment. Process equipment, tanks, silos, pressure pipelines and machine bases are often welded on-site under tight production-downtime constraints. From Konya, ArmaWeld provides end-to-end support to industrial projects through a shop facility and mobile site teams.</p>',
    blog_endustriyel_kaynak_hizmeti_s1: '<h2>1. Types of Industrial Welding</h2><ul><li><strong>Shop welding:</strong> New equipment, spare parts, modular fabrication</li><li><strong>Site welding:</strong> Modification and revamp of existing plants</li><li><strong>Maintenance/repair welding:</strong> Worn equipment repair</li><li><strong>Pipeline welding:</strong> ASME B31.3 and EN 13480 scope</li></ul>',
    blog_endustriyel_kaynak_hizmeti_s2: '<h2>2. Typical Process for a Plant Project</h2><p>An industrial welding project usually flows through scoping, dimensional survey, material procurement, shop prefabrication, site erection and commissioning.</p><table class="data-table"><thead><tr><th>Step</th><th>Typical Output</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Scoping</td><td>Scope and risk assessment</td></tr><tr><td>Survey/3D scan</td><td>As-built model, clash report</td></tr><tr><td>Prefabrication</td><td>Shop-built modules</td></tr><tr><td>Site erection</td><td>On-site welding and alignment</td></tr><tr><td>Inspection</td><td>VT, PT/MT, pressure test</td></tr></tbody></table>',
    blog_endustriyel_kaynak_hizmeti_s3: '<h2>3. Quality and Safety</h2><p>HSE management is at least as important as weld quality on plant sites. ArmaWeld’s site teams comply with hot work permits, gas measurement and PPE requirements per customer procedures. ArmaWeld welders are <span class="tag-inline">EN ISO 9606-1</span> certified and additionally qualified to project-specific tests when needed. All welding records are kept digitally and provided in the delivery package.</p>',
    blog_endustriyel_kaynak_hizmeti_s4: '<h2>4. From Konya to Türkiye-Wide Service</h2><p>From Konya, ArmaWeld provides <strong>industrial welding services</strong> to food, chemical, cement, energy and mining facilities across Türkiye. Turn-key modernization, spare-part fabrication and emergency on-site repairs are part of the service scope. ArmaWeld’s engineering capability allows the project not only to be fabricated but also to be designed and commissioned end-to-end through a single contact.</p>',
    blog_endustriyel_kaynak_hizmeti_cta_h3: 'Industrial welding services for your plant',
    blog_endustriyel_kaynak_hizmeti_cta_p: 'Contact us for shop prefabrication, site welding and modernization projects.',
    blog_endustriyel_kaynak_hizmeti_cta_btn: 'Request a Quote →',

    // 6) kaynak-kalite-kontrol
    blog_kaynak_kalite_kontrol_title: 'Quality Control in Welded Manufacturing: VT, NDT and Traceability | ArmaWeld',
    blog_kaynak_kalite_kontrol_meta_desc: 'Quality control processes in welded manufacturing: visual inspection, NDT methods, acceptance criteria and digital traceability.',
    blog_kaynak_kalite_kontrol_og_title: 'Quality Control in Welded Manufacturing: VT, NDT and Traceability',
    blog_kaynak_kalite_kontrol_tag: 'Quality Control · NDT',
    blog_kaynak_kalite_kontrol_h1: 'Quality Control in Welded Manufacturing: VT, NDT and Traceability',
    blog_kaynak_kalite_kontrol_read: '8 min read',
    blog_kaynak_kalite_kontrol_author: 'ArmaWeld Engineering',
    blog_kaynak_kalite_kontrol_breadcrumb3: 'Quality Control',
    blog_kaynak_kalite_kontrol_s0: '<p>Quality <strong>welded manufacturing</strong> requires far more than producing a good weld: design, material, method, personnel and inspection must be managed inside a disciplined quality system. This article covers visual testing (VT), non-destructive testing (NDT) methods, acceptance criteria and the traceability infrastructure used in welding projects.</p>',
    blog_kaynak_kalite_kontrol_s1: '<h2>1. Visual Testing (VT)</h2><p>VT is the most basic and the first inspection to perform. Per <span class="tag-inline">EN ISO 17637</span>, 100% of every weld is visually inspected. Surface defects, finish geometry, weld size and spatter are evaluated at this stage. At ArmaWeld, VT is performed by EN ISO 9712 Level 2 certified personnel.</p>',
    blog_kaynak_kalite_kontrol_s2: '<h2>2. NDT Methods and Selection</h2><table class="data-table"><thead><tr><th>Method</th><th>Standard</th><th>Typical Use</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>VT</td><td>EN ISO 17637</td><td>All welds</td></tr><tr><td>PT</td><td>EN ISO 3452</td><td>Surface defects (stainless/aluminum)</td></tr><tr><td>MT</td><td>EN ISO 17638</td><td>Surface/near-surface (ferromagnetic)</td></tr><tr><td>UT</td><td>EN ISO 17640</td><td>Volumetric, heavy section</td></tr><tr><td>RT</td><td>EN ISO 17636</td><td>Volumetric, thin–medium section</td></tr></tbody></table>',
    blog_kaynak_kalite_kontrol_s3: '<h2>3. Acceptance Criteria</h2><p>Acceptance criteria depend on the application standard. For structural steel, <span class="tag-inline">EN ISO 5817</span> quality levels B/C/D are used. For pressure equipment, stricter limits apply under PED and EN 13445. Accept/reject decisions are documented by the welding engineer based on NDT reports.</p><div class="callout"><p><strong>Tip:</strong> Acceptance criteria (B/C/D), NDT percentage and reference standard should be locked in at contract stage; this scope drives 20–40% of the quality cost.</p></div>',
    blog_kaynak_kalite_kontrol_s4: '<h2>4. Digital Traceability</h2><p>Digital traceability is a non-negotiable for modern welded manufacturing. In ArmaWeld’s quality infrastructure, every weld is recorded together with welder ID, WPS number, consumable batch, preheat temperature and inspection result. This information is delivered to the customer in a consolidated package, so each weld can be traced back even years later. This setup is often a contractual requirement in defense, pressure equipment and bridge projects.</p>',
    blog_kaynak_kalite_kontrol_cta_h3: 'Welded manufacturing with certified quality',
    blog_kaynak_kalite_kontrol_cta_p: 'Production with EN ISO 3834-2 and EN 1090 plus digital traceability infrastructure.',
    blog_kaynak_kalite_kontrol_cta_btn: 'Request a Quote →',

    // 7) tarim-makinesi-kaynak
    blog_tarim_makinesi_kaynak_title: 'Welded Manufacturing for Agricultural Machinery | ArmaWeld',
    blog_tarim_makinesi_kaynak_meta_desc: 'Welding for agricultural machinery: plows, seeders, trailers, combine chassis fabrication. Subcontract and serial production from Konya-based ArmaWeld.',
    blog_tarim_makinesi_kaynak_og_title: 'Welded Manufacturing for Agricultural Machinery',
    blog_tarim_makinesi_kaynak_tag: 'Agricultural Machinery',
    blog_tarim_makinesi_kaynak_h1: 'Welded Manufacturing for Agricultural Machinery',
    blog_tarim_makinesi_kaynak_read: '7 min read',
    blog_tarim_makinesi_kaynak_author: 'ArmaWeld Engineering',
    blog_tarim_makinesi_kaynak_breadcrumb3: 'Agricultural Machinery',
    blog_tarim_makinesi_kaynak_s0: '<p>Konya is the agricultural machinery capital of Türkiye. Plows, seeders, trailers and combine chassis produced here are exported to Europe, the Middle East and Africa. <strong>Welding for agricultural machinery</strong> requires high volumes, short cycle times and durable results. ArmaWeld supplies welded manufacturing services to OEMs and tier suppliers in Konya.</p>',
    blog_tarim_makinesi_kaynak_s1: '<h2>1. Steels Used in Agricultural Machinery</h2><p>Agricultural equipment usually relies on S355 structural steel, HARDOX 450/500 wear plate and special heat-treated alloys. Wear plates are HARDOX while frame structures are produced from S355 J2 or S420. These different material families require different WPS and consumable strategies.</p>',
    blog_tarim_makinesi_kaynak_s2: '<h2>2. Serial Production Strategies</h2><ul><li><strong>Robotic welding:</strong> high repeatability for identical chassis or sub-parts</li><li><strong>Fixtures/jigs:</strong> reduce tolerance and cycle time</li><li><strong>Synergic MIG/MAG:</strong> reduces operator dependency</li><li><strong>In-cell quality control:</strong> VT on every part plus sampled NDT</li></ul>',
    blog_tarim_makinesi_kaynak_s3: '<h2>3. Typical Agricultural Machinery Components</h2><table class="data-table"><thead><tr><th>Component</th><th>Material</th><th>Process</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Chassis frame</td><td>S355 J2</td><td>MAG (135)</td></tr><tr><td>Wear plates</td><td>HARDOX 450/500</td><td>FCAW (136) + preheat</td></tr><tr><td>Tube/profile</td><td>S275 / S355</td><td>MAG (135)</td></tr><tr><td>Plow shares</td><td>Boron steel</td><td>SMAW (111) repair</td></tr><tr><td>Cabin</td><td>S235 / S275</td><td>MAG / robot</td></tr></tbody></table>',
    blog_tarim_makinesi_kaynak_s4: '<h2>4. ArmaWeld Agricultural Machinery Capacity</h2><p>At the Konya OIZ facility, ArmaWeld produces thousands of chassis and wear parts annually for agricultural machinery. Robotic welding cells and calibrated fixtures deliver high repeatability. Per customer quality requirements, delivery is made to EN ISO 5817 quality level B or C, with surface blasting and electrostatic powder coating included under the same roof.</p>',
    blog_tarim_makinesi_kaynak_cta_h3: 'Serial-production welding for agricultural machinery',
    blog_tarim_makinesi_kaynak_cta_p: 'Get a quote for robotic chassis fabrication and wear-part production.',
    blog_tarim_makinesi_kaynak_cta_btn: 'Request a Quote →',

    // 8) enerji-sektoru-kaynak
    blog_enerji_sektoru_kaynak_title: 'Welded Manufacturing in the Energy Sector: Wind, Solar, Hydro | ArmaWeld',
    blog_enerji_sektoru_kaynak_meta_desc: 'Welded manufacturing for the energy sector: wind turbine components, solar structures, hydroelectric cabinets. EN 1090 + EN ISO 3834-2.',
    blog_enerji_sektoru_kaynak_og_title: 'Welded Manufacturing in the Energy Sector: Wind, Solar, Hydro',
    blog_enerji_sektoru_kaynak_tag: 'Energy Sector',
    blog_enerji_sektoru_kaynak_h1: 'Welded Manufacturing in the Energy Sector: Wind, Solar, Hydro',
    blog_enerji_sektoru_kaynak_read: '8 min read',
    blog_enerji_sektoru_kaynak_author: 'ArmaWeld Engineering',
    blog_enerji_sektoru_kaynak_breadcrumb3: 'Energy Sector',
    blog_enerji_sektoru_kaynak_s0: '<p>Renewable energy investments are growing fast worldwide and in Türkiye. <strong>Welding for the energy sector</strong> — wind turbines, solar structures and hydropower facilities — demands work with high-strength steels under tight quality requirements. ArmaWeld manufactures structural components and cabinets for the energy industry from Konya.</p>',
    blog_enerji_sektoru_kaynak_s1: '<h2>1. Wind Turbine Components</h2><p>In wind turbine production, tower flanges, foundation structures and nacelle internals are welded fabrications. Steels with low-temperature impact toughness such as S355 NL, S420 NL or S460 NL are typically used.</p><ul><li>Tower segments: SAW (121), inside and outside passes</li><li>Flange welds: full-penetration, 100% UT</li><li>Nacelle internal frames: MAG (135) and robotic welding</li></ul>',
    blog_enerji_sektoru_kaynak_s2: '<h2>2. Solar Energy Structures</h2><p>In solar (PV) plants, the main load-bearing structures are typically galvanized S275/S355 sections. Welded manufacturing comes into play in transformer cabinets, monitoring structures and connection details. EN 1090 EXC2 is the standard execution class for these projects.</p>',
    blog_enerji_sektoru_kaynak_s3: '<h2>3. Hydro and Thermal Applications</h2><table class="data-table"><thead><tr><th>Application</th><th>Typical Material</th><th>Process</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Penstock</td><td>S355 / S460</td><td>SAW + UT</td></tr><tr><td>Turbine casing</td><td>P355 / P460</td><td>SAW + RT</td></tr><tr><td>Boiler element</td><td>P265GH / 16Mo3</td><td>TIG root + SAW</td></tr><tr><td>Cooling towers</td><td>S235 / S275</td><td>MAG (135)</td></tr></tbody></table>',
    blog_enerji_sektoru_kaynak_s4: '<h2>4. Quality and Certification</h2><p>For energy projects, EN 1090 EXC2/EXC3, <span class="tag-inline">EN ISO 3834-2</span> and PED 2014/68/EU are typical scopes. For pipes and pressure equipment, every welder is qualified per PQR; SAW machine settings are recorded. ArmaWeld links every weld to its digital traceability infrastructure for energy projects, delivering a complete QC package to the customer.</p>',
    blog_enerji_sektoru_kaynak_cta_h3: 'ArmaWeld for your energy project',
    blog_enerji_sektoru_kaynak_cta_p: 'Welded manufacturing solutions for wind, solar, hydro and thermal projects.',
    blog_enerji_sektoru_kaynak_cta_btn: 'Request a Quote →',

    // 9) robotik-kaynak-uretim
    blog_robotik_kaynak_uretim_title: 'Serial Production with Robotic Welding | ArmaWeld',
    blog_robotik_kaynak_uretim_meta_desc: 'Serial production with robotic welding: repeatability, cycle time, programming and applications. ArmaWeld’s robotic welding cells.',
    blog_robotik_kaynak_uretim_og_title: 'Serial Production with Robotic Welding',
    blog_robotik_kaynak_uretim_tag: 'Robotic Welding · Serial Production',
    blog_robotik_kaynak_uretim_h1: 'Serial Production with Robotic Welding',
    blog_robotik_kaynak_uretim_read: '7 min read',
    blog_robotik_kaynak_uretim_author: 'ArmaWeld Engineering',
    blog_robotik_kaynak_uretim_breadcrumb3: 'Robotic Welding',
    blog_robotik_kaynak_uretim_s0: '<p><strong>Robotic welding</strong> is one of the most important investments for serial-production welded manufacturing companies in terms of productivity, quality repeatability and cost competitiveness. ArmaWeld runs serial production with 6-axis industrial robots in Konya. This article covers the benefits of robotic welding, suitable part geometries and programming workflows.</p>',
    blog_robotik_kaynak_uretim_s1: '<h2>1. Benefits of Robotic Welding</h2><ul><li><strong>Repeatability:</strong> identical welds across all parts</li><li><strong>Productivity:</strong> 3–5× welding time per operator</li><li><strong>Quality:</strong> reduced spatter, finish defects and geometry deviation</li><li><strong>Traceability:</strong> current, voltage and travel speed recorded automatically</li><li><strong>OHS:</strong> operator is not directly exposed to arc, fume or spatter</li></ul>',
    blog_robotik_kaynak_uretim_s2: '<h2>2. Which Parts Suit Robotic Welding?</h2><p>Not all parts are good candidates. The following criteria deliver economic value:</p><ul><li>Volume: 100+ parts/month serial</li><li>Tolerances: laser-cut precision (±0.2–0.5 mm)</li><li>Stable geometry: standard positions over complex 3D paths</li><li>Access: enough clearance for the torch</li></ul>',
    blog_robotik_kaynak_uretim_s3: '<h2>3. Programming and Commissioning</h2><table class="data-table"><thead><tr><th>Step</th><th>Lead Time</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Fixture design</td><td>1–2 weeks</td></tr><tr><td>Robot programming</td><td>2–5 days</td></tr><tr><td>Parameter optimization</td><td>1–3 days</td></tr><tr><td>First Article Inspection (FAI)</td><td>1 day</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Modern robots can correct the path before welding using laser or contact sensors, compensating for sheet thickness or cutting tolerance deviations.</p>',
    blog_robotik_kaynak_uretim_s4: '<h2>4. ArmaWeld Robotic Welding Cells</h2><p>ArmaWeld’s Konya facility includes two 6-axis robotic welding cells. Synergic MIG/MAG power sources and servo torches handle both thin sheet and medium-thickness parts. Tractor and combine sub-frames, defense substructure components and electrical cabinets run through the robotic line. Per customer requirement, all robotic welds are subject to 100% VT and sampled NDT testing.</p>',
    blog_robotik_kaynak_uretim_cta_h3: 'Speed up your serial production with robotic welding',
    blog_robotik_kaynak_uretim_cta_p: 'Contact us for robotic welding feasibility and fixture design.',
    blog_robotik_kaynak_uretim_cta_btn: 'Request a Quote →',

    // 10) paslanmaz-celik-imalat
    blog_paslanmaz_celik_imalat_title: 'Stainless Steel Welded Manufacturing: Food, Pharma, Chemical | ArmaWeld',
    blog_paslanmaz_celik_imalat_meta_desc: 'Stainless steel welded manufacturing: 304/316L welding, food, pharma and chemical applications, surface and hygiene requirements.',
    blog_paslanmaz_celik_imalat_og_title: 'Stainless Steel Welded Manufacturing: Food, Pharma, Chemical',
    blog_paslanmaz_celik_imalat_tag: 'Stainless Steel · Hygienic',
    blog_paslanmaz_celik_imalat_h1: 'Stainless Steel Welded Manufacturing: Food, Pharma, Chemical',
    blog_paslanmaz_celik_imalat_read: '8 min read',
    blog_paslanmaz_celik_imalat_author: 'ArmaWeld Engineering',
    blog_paslanmaz_celik_imalat_breadcrumb3: 'Stainless Steel Manufacturing',
    blog_paslanmaz_celik_imalat_s0: '<p><strong>Stainless steel manufacturing</strong> for the food, pharma, beverage and chemical industries must meet hygiene, corrosion resistance and cleanability requirements. Weld details, surface quality and passivation are typically contract requirements. At ArmaWeld’s Konya facility, welded manufacturing is delivered in 304, 316L and duplex stainless steel.</p>',
    blog_paslanmaz_celik_imalat_s1: '<h2>1. Common Stainless Alloys</h2><table class="data-table"><thead><tr><th>Alloy</th><th>Typical Use</th><th>Filler</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>304/304L</td><td>General food, kitchen</td><td>ER308L</td></tr><tr><td>316/316L</td><td>Pharma, seawater, chemical</td><td>ER316L</td></tr><tr><td>2205 Duplex</td><td>Petrochemical, marine</td><td>ER2209</td></tr><tr><td>904L</td><td>Sulfuric acid, chlorine</td><td>ER385</td></tr></tbody></table>',
    blog_paslanmaz_celik_imalat_s2: '<h2>2. Hygienic Weld Details</h2><p>Food and pharma projects follow EHEDG and 3-A standards which set geometric rules for cleanability. Typical hygienic weld details:</p><ul><li>Internal corner radius ≥ 3 mm</li><li>Smooth full-penetration pipe welds (orbital TIG)</li><li>Internal surface Ra ≤ 0.8 µm</li><li>Passivation of all surfaces (HNO3 or citric acid)</li><li>Complete removal of post-weld heat tint</li></ul>',
    blog_paslanmaz_celik_imalat_s3: '<h2>3. Sensitization and Corrosion</h2><p>Stainless steel held between 450–850°C for prolonged periods may suffer intergranular corrosion due to chromium carbide precipitation (sensitization). Mitigations:</p><div class="callout"><p><strong>Rule of thumb:</strong> Choose low-carbon (≤0.03%) alloys such as 304L/316L, minimize heat input, keep interpass below 150°C, and apply heat treatment when needed.</p></div>',
    blog_paslanmaz_celik_imalat_s4: '<h2>4. ArmaWeld Stainless Production Line</h2><p>ArmaWeld’s Konya facility includes a dedicated stainless production cell. Separate grinding, brushing and tool sets prevent carbon-steel contamination. Tanks, silos, mixers and special process equipment are produced with orbital TIG, manual TIG and pulse MIG. Surface passivation and electropolishing are available on request.</p>',
    blog_paslanmaz_celik_imalat_cta_h3: 'Run your stainless production with ArmaWeld',
    blog_paslanmaz_celik_imalat_cta_p: 'Hygienic welded manufacturing and surface finishing for food, pharma and chemical industries.',
    blog_paslanmaz_celik_imalat_cta_btn: 'Request a Quote →',

    // 11) insaat-celik-imalat
    blog_insaat_celik_imalat_title: 'Welded Steel Fabrication for the Construction Sector | ArmaWeld',
    blog_insaat_celik_imalat_meta_desc: 'Welded steel fabrication for construction: EN 1090 EXC2/EXC3, load-bearing systems, shop and site welding. Konya-based ArmaWeld.',
    blog_insaat_celik_imalat_og_title: 'Welded Steel Fabrication for the Construction Sector',
    blog_insaat_celik_imalat_tag: 'Construction · Structural Steel',
    blog_insaat_celik_imalat_h1: 'Welded Steel Fabrication for the Construction Sector',
    blog_insaat_celik_imalat_read: '7 min read',
    blog_insaat_celik_imalat_author: 'ArmaWeld Engineering',
    blog_insaat_celik_imalat_breadcrumb3: 'Construction Sector',
    blog_insaat_celik_imalat_s0: '<p>The construction sector is one of the heaviest consumers of welded fabrication. Industrial facilities, warehouses, malls, hotels and offices are erected with steel frames. Within <strong>structural steel fabrication</strong>, columns, beams, trusses and connection details are welded both in shop and on site. ArmaWeld manufactures EN 1090 EXC2/EXC3 certified structural steel from its Konya facility.</p>',
    blog_insaat_celik_imalat_s1: '<h2>1. Structural Steel Grades</h2><ul><li><strong>S235/S275:</strong> general construction, light structures</li><li><strong>S355:</strong> industrial primary members</li><li><strong>S420/S460:</strong> high-strength projects</li><li><strong>S355 J0/J2/JR:</strong> selection by impact toughness class</li></ul>',
    blog_insaat_celik_imalat_s2: '<h2>2. EN 1090 EXC Classes for Construction</h2><p>The EXC class is set per structure type and risk level. Typically:</p><table class="data-table"><thead><tr><th>Structure Type</th><th>EXC Class</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Agricultural building, small warehouse</td><td>EXC1</td></tr><tr><td>Industrial building, mall</td><td>EXC2</td></tr><tr><td>Multi-story building, crane runways, bridges</td><td>EXC3</td></tr><tr><td>High-risk structures (stadiums, special)</td><td>EXC4</td></tr></tbody></table>',
    blog_insaat_celik_imalat_s3: '<h2>3. Connection Details</h2><p>Construction steel uses welded (shop), bolted (site) or hybrid connections. For full-penetration welds in shop, joint preparation per EN ISO 9692-1 applies. MAG/FCAW dominates site welding. Bolted connections use preloaded HV bolts per EN 14399.</p>',
    blog_insaat_celik_imalat_s4: '<h2>4. Typical Project Flow</h2><p>Construction steel projects flow through design coordination, shop prefabrication, surface preparation (Sa 2½), painting or galvanizing, logistics and site erection. ArmaWeld ships modules from Konya across Türkiye and to export markets. With site erection coordination, turn-key solutions are delivered.</p>',
    blog_insaat_celik_imalat_cta_h3: 'Get a quote for your construction steel project from Konya',
    blog_insaat_celik_imalat_cta_p: 'Prefabrication and site erection in the EN 1090 EXC2/EXC3 certified shop.',
    blog_insaat_celik_imalat_cta_btn: 'Request a Quote →',

    // 12) zirhli-arac-kaynak
    blog_zirhli_arac_kaynak_title: 'Welding for Armored Vehicles and Defense Platforms | ArmaWeld',
    blog_zirhli_arac_kaynak_meta_desc: 'Armored vehicle welding: STANAG 4569 levels, ARMOX/MARS ballistic steel parameters and ballistic acceptance criteria for welds.',
    blog_zirhli_arac_kaynak_og_title: 'Welding for Armored Vehicles and Defense Platforms',
    blog_zirhli_arac_kaynak_tag: 'Defense · Armored Vehicles',
    blog_zirhli_arac_kaynak_h1: 'Welding for Armored Vehicles and Defense Platforms',
    blog_zirhli_arac_kaynak_read: '9 min read',
    blog_zirhli_arac_kaynak_author: 'ArmaWeld Engineering',
    blog_zirhli_arac_kaynak_breadcrumb3: 'Armored Vehicle Welding',
    blog_zirhli_arac_kaynak_s0: '<p>In armored vehicle production, welds are the weakest link of the ballistic protection envelope, demanding special engineering attention. <strong>Armored vehicle welding</strong> covers ballistic steel selection, narrow heat input windows, austenitic filler metals and often ballistic test panel verification.</p>',
    blog_zirhli_arac_kaynak_s1: '<h2>1. Ballistic Steel Selection</h2><table class="data-table"><thead><tr><th>Brand</th><th>Typical Hardness (HB)</th><th>STANAG Level</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>ARMOX 500T</td><td>480–540</td><td>2–3</td></tr><tr><td>ARMOX 600T</td><td>570–640</td><td>3–4</td></tr><tr><td>MARS 240</td><td>440–500</td><td>2–3</td></tr><tr><td>SECURE 500</td><td>480–540</td><td>2–3</td></tr></tbody></table>',
    blog_zirhli_arac_kaynak_s2: '<h2>2. Welding Parameter Control</h2><p>Manufacturer datasheets are the main reference for welding ballistic steel. Typical control points:</p><ul><li>Maximum heat input: 1.0–1.5 kJ/mm</li><li>Interpass temperature: 150–200°C</li><li>Preheat: 100–150°C depending on thickness</li><li>Filler: austenitic electrodes such as AWS E307, E309LMo</li><li>Hydrogen level: H5 (≤5 ml H₂/100g) or H4</li></ul>',
    blog_zirhli_arac_kaynak_s3: '<h2>3. Ballistic Test Verification</h2><p>For high threat-level welds, ballistic test plates are produced and shot with live ammunition. Acceptance requires no hole growth, cracking or spalling at the weld. ArmaWeld maintains dedicated WPS documentation, consumable batch tracking and operator pairing for welds undergoing ballistic testing.</p>',
    blog_zirhli_arac_kaynak_s4: '<h2>4. ArmaWeld Defense Track Record</h2><p>ArmaWeld manufactures substructure parts and integrated modules for armored vehicles and defense platforms from Konya. All operations run under EN ISO 3834-2 with welding engineer coordination, open to customer and notified body audits. Confidentiality, traceability and delivery discipline are managed at the highest level for defense industry projects.</p>',
    blog_zirhli_arac_kaynak_cta_h3: 'Quote for your armored vehicle substructure project',
    blog_zirhli_arac_kaynak_cta_p: 'Contact us for ballistic steel welding, modular fabrication and serial production.',
    blog_zirhli_arac_kaynak_cta_btn: 'Request a Quote →',

    // 13) boru-profil-imalat
    blog_boru_profil_imalat_title: 'Welded Tube and Section Fabrication | ArmaWeld',
    blog_boru_profil_imalat_meta_desc: 'Welded tube and section fabrication: hollow sections, rectangular tubes, welded pipe production processes and applications.',
    blog_boru_profil_imalat_og_title: 'Welded Tube and Section Fabrication',
    blog_boru_profil_imalat_tag: 'Tubes & Sections',
    blog_boru_profil_imalat_h1: 'Welded Tube and Section Fabrication',
    blog_boru_profil_imalat_read: '7 min read',
    blog_boru_profil_imalat_author: 'ArmaWeld Engineering',
    blog_boru_profil_imalat_breadcrumb3: 'Tubes & Sections',
    blog_boru_profil_imalat_s0: '<p>Welded tube and section products are the main raw material for many sectors including structural steel, machinery and furniture. ArmaWeld provides services for both standard and custom-section welded tube and profile-based fabrication.</p>',
    blog_boru_profil_imalat_s1: '<h2>1. Section Types</h2><ul><li><strong>Hollow sections:</strong> 20×20 to 400×400 in S235/S355</li><li><strong>Rectangular tubes:</strong> structural steel, doors, windows</li><li><strong>Round tubes:</strong> hydraulic cylinders, furniture, railings</li><li><strong>Custom sections:</strong> shaped per customer design</li></ul>',
    blog_boru_profil_imalat_s2: '<h2>2. Welded Tube Production Steps</h2><p>Standard welded tube is produced by roll-forming sheet strips and welding the longitudinal seam (HF or MAG). ArmaWeld procures this semi-finished material and manages cutting, mitre preparation, tacking and final welding end to end.</p>',
    blog_boru_profil_imalat_s3: '<h2>3. Tolerances and Quality</h2><table class="data-table"><thead><tr><th>Property</th><th>Standard</th><th>Tolerance</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Dimension</td><td>EN 10219</td><td>±1%</td></tr><tr><td>Straightness</td><td>EN 10219</td><td>0.2% × L</td></tr><tr><td>Angle/twist</td><td>EN ISO 13920</td><td>Class B</td></tr></tbody></table>',
    blog_boru_profil_imalat_s4: '<h2>4. Typical Applications</h2><p>Welded tube and section fabrication is heavily used in agricultural machinery chassis, trailer skeletons, crane booms and tower structures, railings and stair systems. ArmaWeld delivers products at semi-finished or fully finished stages. Surface preparation, painting or galvanizing are included as a single-source solution.</p>',
    blog_boru_profil_imalat_cta_h3: 'Welded tube and section based fabrication',
    blog_boru_profil_imalat_cta_p: 'Contact us for standard and custom profile processing.',
    blog_boru_profil_imalat_cta_btn: 'Request a Quote →',

    // 14) hidrolik-sistem-imalat
    blog_hidrolik_sistem_imalat_title: 'Welded Manufacturing of Hydraulic and Pneumatic Systems | ArmaWeld',
    blog_hidrolik_sistem_imalat_meta_desc: 'Welded fabrication of hydraulic cylinders, tanks and manifolds: pressure resistance, leak-tightness, NDT and test processes.',
    blog_hidrolik_sistem_imalat_og_title: 'Welded Manufacturing of Hydraulic and Pneumatic Systems',
    blog_hidrolik_sistem_imalat_tag: 'Hydraulic · Pneumatic',
    blog_hidrolik_sistem_imalat_h1: 'Welded Manufacturing of Hydraulic and Pneumatic Systems',
    blog_hidrolik_sistem_imalat_read: '7 min read',
    blog_hidrolik_sistem_imalat_author: 'ArmaWeld Engineering',
    blog_hidrolik_sistem_imalat_breadcrumb3: 'Hydraulic Systems',
    blog_hidrolik_sistem_imalat_s0: '<p>Hydraulic and pneumatic systems are the power-transmission backbone of construction equipment, agricultural machinery, cranes and special machines. <strong>Hydraulic welded manufacturing</strong> requires combined pressure resistance, leak tightness and long service life. ArmaWeld delivers welded fabrication for cylinder bodies, tanks and special manifold structures.</p>',
    blog_hidrolik_sistem_imalat_s1: '<h2>1. Hydraulic Cylinder Production</h2><p>Critical weld details on a hydraulic cylinder body are at the head, base and flange regions. Typical materials include S355J2+N or 27MnCrB5. TIG root with MAG fill is common for full-penetration welds. Test pressure is generally 1.5× operating pressure.</p>',
    blog_hidrolik_sistem_imalat_s2: '<h2>2. Hydraulic Tanks and Reservoirs</h2><p>The main goals for hydraulic tank fabrication are leak tightness and a smooth internal surface. Methods used to detect leaks:</p><ul><li>Air + soap-water test</li><li>Helium leak test (high sensitivity)</li><li>Vacuum test</li><li>Penetrant testing (PT)</li></ul>',
    blog_hidrolik_sistem_imalat_s3: '<h2>3. Manifolds and Special Blocks</h2><table class="data-table"><thead><tr><th>Part</th><th>Process</th><th>NDT</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Cylinder body</td><td>TIG root + MAG</td><td>100% VT, 10% UT</td></tr><tr><td>Tank shell</td><td>MAG (135)</td><td>100% VT, leak test</td></tr><tr><td>Manifold</td><td>TIG (141)</td><td>100% VT, pressure test</td></tr><tr><td>Pipeline</td><td>TIG root + MAG</td><td>100% VT, RT/UT</td></tr></tbody></table>',
    blog_hidrolik_sistem_imalat_s4: '<h2>4. ArmaWeld Hydraulic Capability</h2><p>ArmaWeld manufactures hydraulic tanks, cylinder bodies and manifold parts for construction and agricultural machinery OEMs. The production line includes certified welders, pressure test rigs up to 250 bar and surface coating infrastructure. Konya-based production gives a fast delivery advantage to customer plants across Türkiye.</p>',
    blog_hidrolik_sistem_imalat_cta_h3: 'Quote for hydraulic system fabrication',
    blog_hidrolik_sistem_imalat_cta_p: 'Contact us for cylinder body, tank and manifold production.',
    blog_hidrolik_sistem_imalat_cta_btn: 'Request a Quote →',

    // 15) ce-isaretleme-kaynak
    blog_ce_isaretleme_kaynak_title: 'CE-Marked Welded Manufacturing: EN 1090 and PED | ArmaWeld',
    blog_ce_isaretleme_kaynak_meta_desc: 'CE marking: welded manufacturing requirements and process steps for EN 1090 structural steel and PED 2014/68/EU pressure equipment.',
    blog_ce_isaretleme_kaynak_og_title: 'CE-Marked Welded Manufacturing: EN 1090 and PED',
    blog_ce_isaretleme_kaynak_tag: 'CE · Standards',
    blog_ce_isaretleme_kaynak_h1: 'CE-Marked Welded Manufacturing: EN 1090 and PED',
    blog_ce_isaretleme_kaynak_read: '8 min read',
    blog_ce_isaretleme_kaynak_author: 'ArmaWeld Engineering',
    blog_ce_isaretleme_kaynak_breadcrumb3: 'CE Marking',
    blog_ce_isaretleme_kaynak_s0: '<p>CE marking is mandatory for welded manufacturing companies selling into the European market. CE is obtained against directives based on the product category. <span class="tag-inline">EN 1090</span> for structural steel and <span class="tag-inline">PED 2014/68/EU</span> for pressure equipment are the main reference frameworks.</p>',
    blog_ce_isaretleme_kaynak_s1: '<h2>1. EN 1090 Scope</h2><p>EN 1090 covers CE marking of structural steel and aluminum components. EN 1090-1 covers system/management requirements while EN 1090-2 details fabrication and quality control. EN 1090-2 defines four execution classes from EXC1 to EXC4.</p>',
    blog_ce_isaretleme_kaynak_s2: '<h2>2. PED Scope</h2><p>PED 2014/68/EU is the directive covering pressure vessels, pipes and accessories. Items are classified into risk categories I–IV by maximum allowable pressure (PS), volume (V), fluid group and properties. Categories III and IV use modules such as G or H requiring a notified body.</p>',
    blog_ce_isaretleme_kaynak_s3: '<h2>3. Typical Manufacturer Path</h2><table class="data-table"><thead><tr><th>Step</th><th>EN 1090</th><th>PED</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>System certification</td><td>EN 1090-1 FPC</td><td>Module H/H1 (quality system)</td></tr><tr><td>Welding QMS</td><td>EN ISO 3834-2</td><td>EN ISO 3834-2</td></tr><tr><td>Welding procedure</td><td>WPS/WPQR</td><td>WPS/WPQR</td></tr><tr><td>Personnel</td><td>EN ISO 9606-1</td><td>EN ISO 9606-1</td></tr><tr><td>Notified body</td><td>Manufacturer declaration + audit</td><td>Per module category</td></tr></tbody></table>',
    blog_ce_isaretleme_kaynak_s4: '<h2>4. ArmaWeld’s CE Approach</h2><p>ArmaWeld maintains EN 1090-2 EXC3 structural steel fabrication competence and an EN ISO 3834-2 welding QMS that is audit-ready. ArmaWeld provides technical support to customers in CE certification for export projects and delivers production data, material certificates and test reports as a structured handover package. Production from Konya gives a cost and lead time advantage for customers exporting to Europe.</p>',
    blog_ce_isaretleme_kaynak_cta_h3: 'Your partner for CE-marked production',
    blog_ce_isaretleme_kaynak_cta_p: 'Contact us for welded manufacturing under EN 1090 and PED.',
    blog_ce_isaretleme_kaynak_cta_btn: 'Request a Quote →',

    // 16) maliyet-optimizasyon
    blog_maliyet_optimizasyon_title: 'Cost Optimization in Welded Manufacturing | ArmaWeld',
    blog_maliyet_optimizasyon_meta_desc: 'Cost optimization in welded manufacturing: material efficiency, weld process selection, automation and quality cost control.',
    blog_maliyet_optimizasyon_og_title: 'Cost Optimization in Welded Manufacturing',
    blog_maliyet_optimizasyon_tag: 'Cost · Productivity',
    blog_maliyet_optimizasyon_h1: 'Cost Optimization in Welded Manufacturing',
    blog_maliyet_optimizasyon_read: '7 min read',
    blog_maliyet_optimizasyon_author: 'ArmaWeld Engineering',
    blog_maliyet_optimizasyon_breadcrumb3: 'Cost Optimization',
    blog_maliyet_optimizasyon_s0: '<p>Unit cost in welded manufacturing has six main components: material, labor, consumables, energy, quality control and waste. With the right design and process choices, these can typically be reduced by 15–30%. This article shares cost optimization tips from engineering, production and quality angles.</p>',
    blog_maliyet_optimizasyon_s1: '<h2>1. Cost in Design</h2><ul><li>Minimize weld volume (DfM): right-sized fillet welds rather than oversized</li><li>Standardize sheet thicknesses</li><li>Use laser cutting plus welded alternatives instead of bolted joints</li><li>Consider modular design instead of single folded sheet</li></ul>',
    blog_maliyet_optimizasyon_s2: '<h2>2. Process Selection</h2><table class="data-table"><thead><tr><th>Process</th><th>Productivity</th><th>Typical Use</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>SMAW (111)</td><td>Low</td><td>Site, repair</td></tr><tr><td>MAG (135)</td><td>Medium-high</td><td>General fabrication</td></tr><tr><td>FCAW (136)</td><td>High</td><td>Heavy section</td></tr><tr><td>SAW (121)</td><td>Very high</td><td>Plate, pipe</td></tr><tr><td>Robotic</td><td>Highest</td><td>Serial production</td></tr></tbody></table>',
    blog_maliyet_optimizasyon_s3: '<h2>3. Cost of Quality</h2><p>In most companies, the real cost of quality is far higher than top management sees. Inadequate design, defective production and customer rejects directly impact profit. ArmaWeld monitors first-pass yield (FPY) and uses tools such as root cause analysis and PFMEA to drive improvements.</p><div class="callout"><p><strong>Tip:</strong> Visible cost of quality (NDT, scrap, rework) is the tip of the iceberg. The hidden part is delay penalties, customer loss and brand damage.</p></div>',
    blog_maliyet_optimizasyon_s4: '<h2>4. Automation and Data</h2><p>Robotic welding, laser cutting and digital traceability increase productivity and reduce defect rates. At ArmaWeld’s Konya facility, every weld’s current/voltage curve, welder ID and consumable batch are recorded digitally. This data feeds cost, quality and export certification needs.</p>',
    blog_maliyet_optimizasyon_cta_h3: 'Let us help reduce your production cost',
    blog_maliyet_optimizasyon_cta_p: 'Contact us for design review, process selection and automation support.',
    blog_maliyet_optimizasyon_cta_btn: 'Request a Quote →',

    // 17) hafif-celik-yapi
    blog_hafif_celik_yapi_title: 'Light Welded Steel Structures | ArmaWeld',
    blog_hafif_celik_yapi_meta_desc: 'Light welded steel structures: containers, modular buildings, steel cabin manufacturing. EN 1090 and lightweight solutions.',
    blog_hafif_celik_yapi_og_title: 'Light Welded Steel Structures',
    blog_hafif_celik_yapi_tag: 'Light Structures · Modular',
    blog_hafif_celik_yapi_h1: 'Light Welded Steel Structures',
    blog_hafif_celik_yapi_read: '6 min read',
    blog_hafif_celik_yapi_author: 'ArmaWeld Engineering',
    blog_hafif_celik_yapi_breadcrumb3: 'Light Steel Structures',
    blog_hafif_celik_yapi_s0: '<p>Light welded steel structures are widely used in transportable applications such as containers, modular buildings, prefab cabins and disaster shelters. The main goals are low weight, high strength and fast assembly.</p>',
    blog_hafif_celik_yapi_s1: '<h2>1. Sections Used in Light Structures</h2><ul><li>Hot-rolled HEA/IPE</li><li>Cold-formed C/Z sections</li><li>Closed hollow sections</li><li>Sandwich panels (non-structural)</li></ul>',
    blog_hafif_celik_yapi_s2: '<h2>2. Container and Modular Building Manufacturing</h2><p>20 ft and 40 ft container frames are typically built from S355 angles and sheet panels. Corner castings must be positioned per ISO 668 tolerances. Modular offices and site cabins generally use light steel skeletons clad with sandwich panels.</p>',
    blog_hafif_celik_yapi_s3: '<h2>3. Typical Sizes and Capacity</h2><table class="data-table"><thead><tr><th>Product</th><th>Size</th><th>Weight</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>20 ft container</td><td>6058×2438×2591 mm</td><td>~2,200 kg</td></tr><tr><td>40 ft container</td><td>12192×2438×2591 mm</td><td>~3,800 kg</td></tr><tr><td>Modular office</td><td>6000×2400×2600 mm</td><td>~1,800 kg</td></tr></tbody></table>',
    blog_hafif_celik_yapi_s4: '<h2>4. ArmaWeld Light-Structure Production</h2><p>At the Konya facility, ArmaWeld manufactures special-project containers, generator cabinets, transformer station enclosures and modular cabins. Surface preparation, paint/galvanizing and electrical infrastructure are available as packaged delivery options. Light structures are particularly important for export logistics due to stackability.</p>',
    blog_hafif_celik_yapi_cta_h3: 'Quote for your light steel structure project',
    blog_hafif_celik_yapi_cta_p: 'Contact us for container, cabin and modular building manufacturing.',
    blog_hafif_celik_yapi_cta_btn: 'Request a Quote →',

    // 18) madencilik-ekipman-kaynak
    blog_madencilik_ekipman_kaynak_title: 'Welded Manufacturing for Mining and Construction Equipment | ArmaWeld',
    blog_madencilik_ekipman_kaynak_meta_desc: 'Welding for mining equipment: conveyors, screening, buckets, wear-plate applications. HARDOX welding and wear solutions.',
    blog_madencilik_ekipman_kaynak_og_title: 'Welded Manufacturing for Mining and Construction Equipment',
    blog_madencilik_ekipman_kaynak_tag: 'Mining · Construction Equipment',
    blog_madencilik_ekipman_kaynak_h1: 'Welded Manufacturing for Mining and Construction Equipment',
    blog_madencilik_ekipman_kaynak_read: '7 min read',
    blog_madencilik_ekipman_kaynak_author: 'ArmaWeld Engineering',
    blog_madencilik_ekipman_kaynak_breadcrumb3: 'Mining Equipment',
    blog_madencilik_ekipman_kaynak_s0: '<p>Welded manufacturing for mining and construction equipment is exposed to high wear, impact and fatigue loads. <strong>Welding for mining equipment</strong> aims to maximize wear life, ease of repair and reduced total cost of ownership.</p>',
    blog_madencilik_ekipman_kaynak_s1: '<h2>1. Wear-Plate Applications</h2><p>HARDOX 400/450/500 and 600 hardness classes are typical mining choices. Wear plates are used in buckets, dozer blades, conveyor screws and screening tables. Controlled preheat and low-hydrogen consumables are mandatory before welding.</p>',
    blog_madencilik_ekipman_kaynak_s2: '<h2>2. Typical Components</h2><table class="data-table"><thead><tr><th>Part</th><th>Material</th><th>Process</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Bucket</td><td>HARDOX 450</td><td>FCAW (136)</td></tr><tr><td>Conveyor frame</td><td>S355 J2</td><td>MAG (135)</td></tr><tr><td>Screening table</td><td>HARDOX 500</td><td>FCAW + preheat</td></tr><tr><td>Crusher jaw plate</td><td>Mn steel</td><td>Special electrode repair</td></tr></tbody></table>',
    blog_madencilik_ekipman_kaynak_s3: '<h2>3. Repair/Refurbishment Service</h2><p>Repair and refurbishment of worn parts is just as valuable as new fabrication for mining customers. ArmaWeld provides wear-plate cladding for excavator buckets, dozer blade refurbishment and conveyor frame repair. Hardfacing and chocky bar applications are common solutions.</p>',
    blog_madencilik_ekipman_kaynak_s4: '<h2>4. ArmaWeld Mining Capability</h2><p>The Konya facility includes dedicated preheat infrastructure and low-hydrogen consumable stock for wear-plate welding. Site repair teams can respond to mining operations across Türkiye. All applications are documented under EN ISO 3834-2 and delivered with the customer’s handover file.</p>',
    blog_madencilik_ekipman_kaynak_cta_h3: 'Production from Konya for your mining project',
    blog_madencilik_ekipman_kaynak_cta_p: 'Contact us for wear-plate fabrication, repair and refurbishment.',
    blog_madencilik_ekipman_kaynak_cta_btn: 'Request a Quote →',

    // 19) fason-kaynak-konya
    blog_fason_kaynak_konya_title: 'What Is Subcontract Welding? Benefits and Process | ArmaWeld',
    blog_fason_kaynak_konya_meta_desc: 'What is subcontract welding and why do OEMs outsource welded fabrication? Benefits, the step-by-step production process and why Konya works well for it.',
    blog_fason_kaynak_konya_og_title: 'What Is Subcontract Welding? Benefits and the Production Process',
    blog_fason_kaynak_konya_tag: 'Subcontract · Welding',
    blog_fason_kaynak_konya_h1: 'What Is Subcontract Welding? Benefits and the Production Process',
    blog_fason_kaynak_konya_read: '6 min read',
    blog_fason_kaynak_konya_author: 'ArmaWeld Engineering',
    blog_fason_kaynak_konya_breadcrumb3: 'Subcontract Welding',
    blog_fason_kaynak_konya_s0: '<p><strong>Subcontract welding</strong> is the welded fabrication service performed against the customer’s design and requirements. OEMs use subcontract production for capacity flexibility and to avoid mixing special products with their core lines. From Konya, ArmaWeld provides subcontract welded fabrication to OEMs in Türkiye and abroad.</p>',
    blog_fason_kaynak_konya_s1: '<h2>1. Benefits of Subcontract Production</h2><ul><li>Variable cost instead of fixed cost</li><li>Capacity flexibility and quick response to seasonal demand</li><li>Serial production without dedicated know-how</li><li>Product portfolio expansion without equipment investment</li></ul>',
    blog_fason_kaynak_konya_s2: '<h2>2. Subcontract Production Flow</h2><p>Professional subcontract production is a disciplined process from contract to handover.</p><table class="data-table"><thead><tr><th>Step</th><th>Output</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Technical alignment</td><td>Drawings, tolerances, BOM</td></tr><tr><td>Sample production</td><td>First Article Inspection (FAI)</td></tr><tr><td>Serial production</td><td>Monthly/weekly batches</td></tr><tr><td>Quality records</td><td>VT, NDT, dimensional reports</td></tr><tr><td>Delivery</td><td>Logistics + documentation</td></tr></tbody></table>',
    blog_fason_kaynak_konya_s3: '<h2>3. The Konya Subcontract Advantage</h2><p>Konya is one of the strongest metalworking hubs in Türkiye. Quick access to sub-industries, raw materials and skilled labor makes it an ideal ecosystem for subcontract production. ArmaWeld treats confidentiality, traceability and delivery discipline as top priorities.</p>',
    blog_fason_kaynak_konya_s4: '<h2>4. ArmaWeld Subcontract Approach</h2><p>ArmaWeld builds long-term, framework-contracted partnerships with subcontract customers. All procedures used in production are documented under EN ISO 3834-2; customer-specific quality requirements (e.g. armor acceptance tests, pressure tests) are integrated when required. ArmaWeld also supports customers exporting from Konya in CE certification.</p>',
    blog_fason_kaynak_konya_cta_h3: 'Your subcontract welding partner in Konya',
    blog_fason_kaynak_konya_cta_p: 'Let us evaluate subcontract welded fabrication proposals for your OEM needs.',
    blog_fason_kaynak_konya_cta_btn: 'Request a Quote →',

    // 20) kaynak-muhendisi-rolu
    blog_kaynak_muhendisi_rolu_title: 'The Role of the Welding Engineer in Welded Manufacturing Projects | ArmaWeld',
    blog_kaynak_muhendisi_rolu_meta_desc: 'Welding engineer (IWE/EWE) responsibilities: WPS/PQR management, quality coordination, EN ISO 14731 and project duties.',
    blog_kaynak_muhendisi_rolu_og_title: 'The Role of the Welding Engineer in Welded Manufacturing Projects',
    blog_kaynak_muhendisi_rolu_tag: 'Welding Engineer · IWE',
    blog_kaynak_muhendisi_rolu_h1: 'The Role of the Welding Engineer in Welded Manufacturing Projects',
    blog_kaynak_muhendisi_rolu_read: '7 min read',
    blog_kaynak_muhendisi_rolu_author: 'ArmaWeld Engineering',
    blog_kaynak_muhendisi_rolu_breadcrumb3: 'Welding Engineer',
    blog_kaynak_muhendisi_rolu_s0: '<p>In a welded manufacturing company, success in quality, productivity and certification largely depends on the welding engineer (IWE/EWE) role. <span class="tag-inline">EN ISO 14731</span> defines the responsibility areas of the welding coordinator clearly.</p>',
    blog_kaynak_muhendisi_rolu_s1: '<h2>1. Duties of the Welding Engineer</h2><ul><li>Preparation and approval of WPS/PQR</li><li>Consumable selection and storage control</li><li>Personnel qualification and training</li><li>QC plan and NDT management</li><li>Technical coordination with customers and notified bodies</li><li>Root cause analysis and corrective action</li></ul>',
    blog_kaynak_muhendisi_rolu_s2: '<h2>2. Education and Certification</h2><p>In Europe, the IWE certificate is issued by IIW/EWF accredited bodies (e.g. GSI, Forman). In Türkiye, this is delivered by AGUB and TÜBİTAK. Companies under EN ISO 3834-2 full quality requirements must appoint a coordinator at IWE level.</p>',
    blog_kaynak_muhendisi_rolu_s3: '<h2>3. The Engineer’s Role Across Project Phases</h2><table class="data-table"><thead><tr><th>Phase</th><th>Engineer Output</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Bid</td><td>Technical feasibility + risk analysis</td></tr><tr><td>Design review</td><td>Weld details, material suitability</td></tr><tr><td>Production</td><td>WPS, PQR, training and audit</td></tr><tr><td>Quality</td><td>NDT plan, accept/reject decisions</td></tr><tr><td>Delivery</td><td>QC dossier, customer reporting</td></tr></tbody></table>',
    blog_kaynak_muhendisi_rolu_s4: '<h2>4. ArmaWeld Engineering Setup</h2><p>ArmaWeld’s structure includes IWE-level welding engineers and EN ISO 9712 certified NDT personnel. ArmaWeld runs design review, WPS management, quality coordination and documentation in customer projects from one source. This setup delivers both quality and lead-time advantages to customers.</p>',
    blog_kaynak_muhendisi_rolu_cta_h3: 'Engineering-driven welded manufacturing',
    blog_kaynak_muhendisi_rolu_cta_p: 'Let us run your project with IWE-level engineering coordination.',
    blog_kaynak_muhendisi_rolu_cta_btn: 'Request a Quote →'

  });

